{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"future-fibroid-hammerkop","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py::test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count`\nfailed once in a full `-m \"not integration and not external\" -n 3 --dist worksteal\n--timeout=300` run and passed in three other full runs of the same suite on the same\nmachine, on trees that differ only in unrelated test files. It is order-dependent,\nnot deterministic.\n\nThe failure:\n\n```\nAssertionError: ['_apply_inbound_update: declining the inbound removal of b...']\n```\n\nThe test asserts a SUMMARY line, `\"declined 1 inbound link removal\"`. What caplog\nactually held was the PER-ITEM line, `\"declining the inbound removal of ...\"`. So\nthe per-item path ran but the summary never fired.\n\n## Evidence for the mechanism\n\nIn `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py`, the summary is\nemitted under `if declined:` (line ~788), and `declined` is only incremented at\nline ~763 in this branch:\n\n```python\nelif confirm_store is not None and not confirm_store.is_confirmed(\n    local_id, target_local_id, relation\n):\n    declined += 1\n```\n\nSo when `confirm_store` is `None`, the removal is still declined and still logged\nper-item, but `declined` stays `0` and the summary is skipped — exactly the observed\noutput. That makes `confirm_store` resolution the suspect, and it is state that can\nplausibly differ depending on what ran earlier in the same xdist worker.\n\nNot reproduced by running `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` alone under\n`-n 3 --dist worksteal` three times (2575 passed each time), nor by running the\nmodule alone (10 passed). So the contaminating test is OUTSIDE that subtree, which\nis consistent with a worker-shared state leak rather than a bug local to the module.\n\n## Why this is filed rather than fixed\n\nFound while landing the four test-infrastructure bugs under the same audit parent.\nIt is not caused by any of them: the run that failed carried only a change to\n`tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py`, the test predates all four\n(`4010da6493`, \"Decline removals of never-confirmed peer links\"), and it passed in\ntwo earlier full-suite runs of this batch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The order dependency is identified: name the test (or shared state) whose\n      earlier execution in the same worker changes `confirm_store` resolution,\n      demonstrated by a reproducible two-test invocation that fails.\n- [ ] The test passes deterministically under `-n 3 --dist worksteal` across at\n      least 10 consecutive full-suite runs, or the underlying state leak is fixed so\n      ordering cannot affect it.\n- [ ] It is decided and recorded whether `declined` failing to count a decline when\n      `confirm_store is None` is itself a production defect (an operator-visible\n      summary silently under-reporting) or correct-by-design, since the assertion\n      only holds when a confirm store exists.","id":"9151-907b-471d-4a38","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","tests","flaky"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Inbound decline-count test is order-dependent under xdist"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786610490799099001,"uuid":"1dbacaec-6b68-4432-a0f1-affdae1cbb53"}